# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group operator terms: use the operator structure for the latest version of Qiskit Fermions"
msgstr "Kelompokkan suku operator: manfaatkan struktur operator untuk versi terbaru Qiskit Fermions"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group operator terms: use the operator structure"
msgstr "Kelompokkan suku operator: manfaatkan struktur operator"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"grouping-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group operator terms: use the operator structure {#group-operator-terms-use-the-operator-structure}"
msgstr "Kelompokkan suku operator: manfaatkan struktur operator {#group-operator-terms-use-the-operator-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Grouping is one of the operations under [`qiskit_fermions.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms#module-qiskit_fermions.operators.terms \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms\"), which collects routines that partition the terms of an operator based on their structure.\n"
msgstr "Pengelompokan adalah salah satu operasi di bawah [`qiskit_fermions.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms#module-qiskit_fermions.operators.terms \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms\"), yang mengumpulkan rutin-rutin untuk mempartisi suku-suku operator berdasarkan strukturnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As described in the [operators guide](operators#term-grouping), operators can store a **groups array**, an optional part of the sparse data structure that associates each term with a group index. Terms sharing the same group index form a group. This lets you use systematically use of the structure in downstream processing.\n"
msgstr "Seperti dijelaskan di [panduan operator](operators#term-grouping), operator bisa menyimpan **groups array**, bagian opsional dari struktur data sparse yang mengaitkan tiap suku dengan indeks grup. Suku-suku dengan indeks grup yang sama membentuk satu grup. Ini memungkinkanmu memanfaatkan struktur tersebut secara sistematis di pemrosesan selanjutnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By grouping related terms (whether by physical properties, algebraic relationships, or problem-specific symmetries), you can unlock several benefits:\n"
msgstr "Dengan mengelompokkan suku-suku yang berkaitan (entah berdasarkan sifat fisik, hubungan aljabar, atau simetri khusus masalah), kamu bisa mendapatkan beberapa manfaat:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Optimized circuit synthesis**: Grouped terms carry problem-specific information through the stack, enabling simpler optimization of the synthesized circuits. This results in reduced circuit depth and gate count.\n"
msgstr "**Sintesis circuit yang dioptimalkan**: Suku yang dikelompokkan membawa informasi khusus masalah sepanjang stack, sehingga optimasi circuit hasil sintesis jadi lebih mudah. Hasilnya, depth circuit dan jumlah gate berkurang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Physical structure preservation**: Groups encode meaningful structure from the original problem (for example, interaction patterns or symmetries) that can be used for more physically meaningful decompositions.\n"
msgstr "**Struktur fisik tetap terjaga**: Grup menyandikan struktur bermakna dari masalah aslinya (misalnya pola interaksi atau simetri) yang bisa dipakai untuk dekomposisi yang lebih bermakna secara fisik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Flow set selection**: Grouping can naturally encode flow sets and other graph-theoretic structures relevant to quantum simulation, as shown in <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id3).\n"
msgstr "**Pemilihan flow set**: Pengelompokan secara alami bisa menyandikan flow set dan struktur teori graf lain yang relevan untuk simulasi kuantum, seperti ditunjukkan di <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id3).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Improved algorithmic stability**: As demonstrated in the [SqDRIFT routine](sqdrift#sqdrift-getting-started), some algorithms can benefit from improved stability or performance due to the preservation of physical properties.\n"
msgstr "**Stabilitas algoritma yang lebih baik**: Seperti ditunjukkan di [rutin SqDRIFT](sqdrift#sqdrift-getting-started), beberapa algoritma bisa mendapat manfaat berupa stabilitas atau performa yang lebih baik berkat terjaganya sifat-sifat fisik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Product-formula factors**: A fermionic product formula splits an operator into its groups, so the grouping determines both the cost and the Trotter error of a time evolution. See [Synthesize an Evolution gate in fermionic space](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation).\n"
msgstr "**Faktor product-formula**: Product formula fermionik memecah operator menjadi grup-grupnya, jadi pengelompokan menentukan biaya sekaligus error Trotter dari sebuah evolusi waktu. Lihat [Sintesis Evolution gate di ruang fermionik](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Usage {#usage}"
msgstr "Penggunaan {#usage}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simplest way to define an operator grouping is by setting the target operator’s `groups` attribute. Below is an example for grouping terms according to the *line flow sets* as shown in Figure 1c of <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[1\\]](#id3).\n"
msgstr "Cara paling sederhana untuk mendefinisikan pengelompokan operator adalah dengan mengatur atribut `groups` dari operator target. Di bawah ini contoh pengelompokan suku berdasarkan *line flow set* seperti pada Gambar 1c di <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[1\\]](#id3).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Hint\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The `qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.grouping` module provides convenience methods for automatically identifying structure in an operator and assigning group indices accordingly.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Petunjuk\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Modul `qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.grouping` menyediakan metode praktis untuk mengidentifikasi struktur dalam operator secara otomatis dan memberi indeks grup yang sesuai.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A simple directed graph on which to define a MajoranaOperator.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/grouping-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A simple directed graph on which to define a MajoranaOperator.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/grouping-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is a simple two-by-three lattice of Majorana modes connected by directed edges. Each edge represents a term in the operator acting on the two connected modes. The goal is to group these terms according to their edge labels (shown on the graph). Terms connected by edges with the same label are placed in the same group. The following code shows how that can be done:\n"
msgstr "Ini adalah lattice dua kali tiga dari mode Majorana yang dihubungkan oleh edge berarah. Tiap edge mewakili satu suku dalam operator yang bekerja pada dua mode yang terhubung. Tujuannya adalah mengelompokkan suku-suku ini berdasarkan label edge-nya (ditampilkan di graf). Suku yang dihubungkan oleh edge berlabel sama ditempatkan di grup yang sama. Kode berikut menunjukkan caranya:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs group=\"code\">\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"PYTHON\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs group=\"code\">\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"PYTHON\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import MajoranaOperator\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Construct operator directly using sparse arrays\n"
"    >>> # 7 terms, each with coefficient 1.0, modes from edge endpoints\n"
"    >>> op = MajoranaOperator(\n"
"    ...     coeffs=[1.0] * 7,\n"
"    ...     modes=[node for edge in edges for node in edge],\n"
"    ...     boundaries=[0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14],\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Assign group indices to terms (groups is part of the sparse data structure)\n"
"    >>> op.groups = groups\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Partition operator by groups\n"
"    >>> grouped_ops = op.split_out_groups()\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Inspect each group\n"
"    >>> for i, g in enumerate(grouped_ops):\n"
"    ...     print(f\"Group {i}: {list(sorted(g.iter_terms()))}\")\n"
"    Group 0: [([0, 1], (1+0j)), ([1, 2], (1+0j))]\n"
"    Group 1: [([3, 0], (1+0j)), ([5, 2], (1+0j))]\n"
"    Group 2: [([1, 4], (1+0j))]\n"
"    Group 3: [([4, 3], (1+0j)), ([5, 4], (1+0j))]\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <TabItem value=\"c\" label=\"C\">\n"
msgstr "  <TabItem value=\"c\" label=\"C\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    #include <qiskit_fermions.h>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    uint64_t num_terms = 7;\n"
"    uint64_t num_modes = 14;\n"
"    uint32_t modes[14] = {0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 0, 1, 4, 5, 2, 5, 4, 4, 3};\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[7] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0},\n"
"                             {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[8] = {0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14};\n"
"    QfMajoranaOperator *op = qf_maj_op_new(num_terms, num_modes, coeffs, modes, boundaries);\n"
msgstr ""
"    uint64_t num_terms = 7;\n"
"    uint64_t num_modes = 14;\n"
"    uint32_t modes[14] = {0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 0, 1, 4, 5, 2, 5, 4, 4, 3};\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[7] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0},\n"
"                             {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[8] = {0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14};\n"
"    QfMajoranaOperator *op = qf_maj_op_new(num_terms, num_modes, coeffs, modes, boundaries);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    uint32_t groups[7] = {0, 0, 1, 2, 1, 3, 3};\n"
"    qf_maj_op_set_groups(op, groups, num_terms);\n"
msgstr ""
"    uint32_t groups[7] = {0, 0, 1, 2, 1, 3, 3};\n"
"    qf_maj_op_set_groups(op, groups, num_terms);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    QfMajoranaOperator *group_ops[4];\n"
"    qf_maj_op_split_out_groups(op, NULL, 0, group_ops);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    QfMajoranaOperator *group_ops[4];\n"
"    qf_maj_op_split_out_groups(op, NULL, 0, group_ops);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analyze a grouping {#analyze-a-grouping}"
msgstr "Menganalisis sebuah pengelompokan {#analyze-a-grouping}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Groups prescribe no meaning of their own: the groups array records which terms belong together, never why. No routine in this library reports whether a grouping is “correct”, because there is no single notion of correctness to report against. Downstream consumers do, however, assume properties of a grouping, and the functions in this section let you check such an assumption up front rather than paying for it on every call.\n"
msgstr "Grup tidak punya makna sendiri: groups array hanya mencatat suku mana yang termasuk bersama, bukan alasannya. Tidak ada rutin di library ini yang melaporkan apakah sebuah pengelompokan itu \"benar\", karena memang tidak ada satu pengertian kebenaran yang bisa dijadikan acuan. Meski begitu, konsumen di hilir mengasumsikan sifat-sifat tertentu dari pengelompokan, dan fungsi-fungsi di bagian ini memungkinkanmu memeriksa asumsi semacam itu di awal, alih-alih membayarnya di setiap pemanggilan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The most common convention is that each group is separately Hermitian. That is what makes fermionic randomized product formulas possible at all: a lone $a^\\dagger_p a_q$ with $p \\neq q$ is not Hermitian, so its time evolution is not unitary and it cannot be sampled on its own. Pairing it with $a^\\dagger_q a_p$ yields a group that can be.\n"
msgstr "Konvensi yang paling umum adalah bahwa setiap grup bersifat Hermitian secara terpisah. Inilah yang membuat product formula acak fermionik mungkin dilakukan: suku $a^\\dagger_p a_q$ sendirian dengan $p \\neq q$ tidak Hermitian, jadi evolusi waktunya tidak unitary dan tidak bisa di-sampling sendiri. Memasangkannya dengan $a^\\dagger_q a_p$ menghasilkan grup yang bisa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import FermionOperator\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.grouping import (\n"
"    ...     group_coeff_means,\n"
"    ...     groups_are_hermitian,\n"
"    ...     groups_have_uniform_coeffs,\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # a conjugate pair, plus one unpaired term. The operator is built from the sparse\n"
"    >>> # arrays rather than from a dictionary, because only the former fixes the term order\n"
"    >>> # that the group indices below are paired with.\n"
"    >>> pair_and_single = FermionOperator(\n"
"    ...     [1.0, 1.0, 1.0],\n"
"    ...     [True, False, True, False, True, False],\n"
"    ...     [0, 1, 1, 0, 2, 3],\n"
"    ...     [0, 2, 4, 6],\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>> pair_and_single.groups = [0, 0, 1]\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> groups_are_hermitian(pair_and_single)  # group 1 is unpaired\n"
"    [True, False]\n"
"    >>> group_coeff_means(pair_and_single)\n"
"    [1.0, 1.0]\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    uint64_t num_terms = 3;\n"
"    uint64_t num_actions = 6;\n"
"    bool actions[6] = {true, false, true, false, true, false};\n"
"    uint32_t modes[6] = {0, 1, 1, 0, 2, 3};\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[3] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[4] = {0, 2, 4, 6};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op =\n"
"        qf_ferm_op_new(num_terms, num_actions, coeffs, actions, modes, boundaries);\n"
msgstr ""
"    uint64_t num_terms = 3;\n"
"    uint64_t num_actions = 6;\n"
"    bool actions[6] = {true, false, true, false, true, false};\n"
"    uint32_t modes[6] = {0, 1, 1, 0, 2, 3};\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[3] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[4] = {0, 2, 4, 6};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op =\n"
"        qf_ferm_op_new(num_terms, num_actions, coeffs, actions, modes, boundaries);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    uint32_t groups[3] = {0, 0, 1};\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_set_groups(op, groups, num_terms);\n"
msgstr ""
"    uint32_t groups[3] = {0, 0, 1};\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_set_groups(op, groups, num_terms);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    bool hermitian[2];\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_groups_are_hermitian(op, 1e-8, hermitian);\n"
msgstr ""
"    bool hermitian[2];\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_groups_are_hermitian(op, 1e-8, hermitian);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    double means[2];\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_group_coeff_means(op, means);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    double means[2];\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_group_coeff_means(op, means);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "One group index per term is enforced {#one-group-index-per-term-is-enforced}"
msgstr "Satu indeks grup per suku diberlakukan secara ketat {#one-group-index-per-term-is-enforced}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The groups array holds one index per term, and assigning one of a different length raises. Nothing downstream re-checks the invariant, so it is enforced where the indices enter the operator: an array that is too short would silently drop trailing terms, and one that is too long would invent groups that no term carries.\n"
msgstr "Groups array menyimpan satu indeks per suku, dan menetapkan array dengan panjang berbeda akan memunculkan error. Tidak ada yang memeriksa ulang invarian ini di hilir, jadi invarian ini dijaga di titik indeks masuk ke operator: array yang terlalu pendek akan diam-diam membuang suku di bagian akhir, dan yang terlalu panjang akan mengarang grup yang tidak dimiliki suku mana pun.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clearing the group indices by assigning `None` is always allowed.\n"
msgstr "Menghapus indeks grup dengan menetapkan `None` selalu diperbolehkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two checks are independent {#the-two-checks-are-independent}"
msgstr "Kedua pemeriksaan itu independen {#the-two-checks-are-independent}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`groups_have_uniform_coeffs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-have-uniform-coeffs#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs\") reports whether a group’s coefficients agree, which is the assumption [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") makes when it averages magnitudes. It is not a weaker form of the Hermiticity check: neither check implies the other, in either direction.\n"
msgstr "[`groups_have_uniform_coeffs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-have-uniform-coeffs#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs\") melaporkan apakah koefisien dalam satu grup sama, yang merupakan asumsi yang dibuat [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") saat merata-ratakan magnitudo. Ini bukan versi yang lebih lemah dari pemeriksaan Hermitian: tidak ada satu pemeriksaan pun yang menyiratkan yang lain, ke arah mana pun.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default the magnitudes are compared, because that is what [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") averages. A Hermitian conjugate pair with complex coefficients has equal magnitudes but unequal coefficients, so it satisfies only the default form.\n"
msgstr "Secara default, magnitudo yang dibandingkan, karena itulah yang dirata-ratakan oleh [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\"). Pasangan konjugat Hermitian dengan koefisien kompleks punya magnitudo yang sama tapi koefisien yang tidak sama, jadi hanya memenuhi bentuk default.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") inherits the one-sided guarantee of [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\"): a `True` entry is always reliable, while a `False` entry is reliable only for operator types whose normal form is a genuine canonical form. Consult the specific operator type to find out which applies.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") mewarisi jaminan satu sisi dari [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\"): entri `True` selalu bisa diandalkan, sedangkan entri `False` hanya bisa diandalkan untuk tipe operator yang normal form-nya benar-benar bentuk kanonik. Cek tipe operator yang spesifik untuk tahu mana yang berlaku.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

